---
<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap" data-core-duration="45–55 minutes" data-extension-duration="15–20 minutes">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Vocabulary · Lesson {page.sequence}</p>
  <h1>Hobbies &amp; <em>free time</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Learn complete activity chunks such as <span class="ex">play chess</span>, <span class="ex">go hiking</span>, <span class="ex">do yoga</span>, <span class="ex">read books</span>, and <span class="ex">listen to music</span>. Then distinguish a routine, a preference, an ability, a present interest, and a question about availability.</p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">45–55 min core</span>
    <span class="tag">play · go · do · other activity verbs</span>
    <span class="tag">routine · preference · ability · availability</span>
    <span class="tag">15–20 min optional listening and retrieval</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Compare activity chunks and speaker meanings.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>Choose forms from the intended message.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Match chunks and ask useful questions.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Recommend activities from fictional profiles.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line"><span class="ex">Free time</span> is uncountable: <span class="ex">I have some free time</span>, not <span class="ex">a free time</span>. A <span class="ex">hobby</span> is an activity or interest someone chooses regularly. <span class="ex">Free-time activity</span> is broader, and natural U.S. questions include <span class="ex">What do you do for fun?</span> and <span class="ex">What do you like to do in your free time?</span></p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You retrieved known-object reference, third-person agreement, and frequency placement.">
    <h3>Three quick checks from earlier lessons</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Answer from memory, then check. Say each complete sentence aloud.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Earlier lesson choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="It is">It is</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="There is">There is</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="plays">plays</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="play">play</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="usually">usually</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="is usually">is usually</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The previous sentence introduced one chess table. Now locate the same table: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="It is" data-hint="The singular table is already known, so refer back with it." data-fix="It is next to the window." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> next to the window.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Maya’s Saturday profile describes her routine: She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="plays" data-hint="A present-simple routine with she adds s to play." data-fix="She plays chess on Saturdays." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> chess on Saturdays.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The card says this happens on most weekends: Maya <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="usually" data-hint="With the main verb plays, usually goes before that verb." data-fix="Maya usually plays chess on Saturdays." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> plays chess on Saturdays.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Meet the activity vocabulary</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>This is an optional word bank, not a list of activities every learner should do. Activities differ in cost, access, energy, location, and social setting. Use fictional choices in practice, and describe personal interests only when you freely choose.</p>
  <div class="figure-grid">
